{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Behold, etc.</b> Rabbi Jonah said: הן גור יגור is like חבור, and he cited כי כמוהו נהרסו ממגורות (Joel 1:17), and the meaning: is it conceivable that a band be joined except by my permission? And the meaning concerns Gog and Magog:" "<b>Whoever gathers to you.</b> Its meaning: whoever joined and was with you and turned against you — he shall fall. But the correct view in my eyes is that גור יגור is according to its standard usage, and so it is: is it conceivable that a sojourner sojourning with you in a land that is mine [would do so] except by my permission? Whoever wishes to sojourn with you in my land — upon you he shall fall, as in אל הכשדי' אתה נופל (Jeremiah 37:13), על פני כל אחיו נפל (Genesis 25:18). And the meaning: he shall throw himself under your authority."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 54, :notes {1 "The bracketed correction צ״ל שיפיל indicates the text should read 'he shall cause to fall'; I translate according to the corrected reading, reflected in 'he shall throw himself.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:59:35.996226640Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}